layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Quieto Design System
description: Design tokens and web components that share one source of truth, in light and dark.
hideTitle: true
toc: false
---

{#
  Laid out as Mantine's home page is: a hero with the numbers that matter, the
  AI tools, then one band per thing the system does well, each with a live demo,
  and how to start.
#}

<section class="hero">
  <p class="hero__eyebrow">
    <qds-chip variant="info">@quieto/ui {{ packages.ui.version }}</qds-chip>
    <a href="/roadmap/">See what is coming next</a>
  </p>
  <h1 class="hero__title">Quieto Design System</h1>
  <p class="hero__lede">
    Design tokens and web components that share one source of truth. Every color,
    space, and type style is a token; every component is styled by nothing else.
  </p>
  <qds-stack direction="inline" gap="300" wrap>
    <a class="hero__action" href="/components/">Browse components</a>
    <a class="hero__action" href="/foundations/tokens/">Read about tokens</a>
  </qds-stack>

  <dl class="hero-stats">
    <div><dt>Components</dt><dd>{{ docs.families | length }}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Design tokens</dt><dd>{{ tokens.stats.total }}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Themes</dt><dd>Light and dark</dd></div>
    <div><dt>License</dt><dd>MIT</dd></div>
  </dl>
</section>

<section class="home-band home-band--ai">
  <h2>Built for AI-assisted work</h2>
  <p class="home-band__lede">
    Ask your assistant for a token system and it can build one: accessible color
    ramps, spacing and type scales, and light and dark themes, checked for
    contrast as it goes.
  </p>
  <ul class="card-grid">
    <li>
      <qds-card class="link-card" variant="elevated">
        <h3 slot="header"><a href="/ai/mcp/">MCP server</a></h3>
        <p>
          {{ ai.mcp.tools | length }} tools for any MCP client, hosted at
          <code>quieto.dev/mcp</code>. Nothing to install.
        </p>
      </qds-card>
    </li>
    <li>
      <qds-card class="link-card" variant="elevated">
        <h3 slot="header"><a href="/ai/skills/">Skills</a></h3>
        <p>
          {{ ai.skills | length }} Claude Code skills that scaffold, audit,
          migrate, and update a token system.
        </p>
      </qds-card>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <pre><code>claude mcp add quieto --transport http {{ ai.mcp.url }}</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="home-band">
  <h2>Explore the docs</h2>
  <ul class="card-grid card-grid--sections">
    {% for section in docs.sections %}
      <li>
        <qds-card class="link-card" variant="elevated">
          <h3 slot="header"><a href="{{ section.url }}">{{ section.title }}</a></h3>
          <p>{{ section.summary }}</p>
          <p slot="footer" class="link-card__meta">
            {% if section.key == 'foundations' %}
              {{ tokens.stats.total }} tokens in three tiers
            {% elif section.key == 'styles' %}
              Color, typography, and icons
            {% elif section.key == 'ai' %}
              MCP server and skills
            {% else %}
              {{ docs.families | length }} components
            {% endif %}
          </p>
        </qds-card>
      </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="home-band">
  <h2>{{ docs.families | length }} components, built from its own parts</h2>
  <p class="home-band__lede">
    This site is the system's first consumer. Its pages are laid out with
    <code>qds-stack</code> and <code>qds-card</code>, search is a
    <code>qds-modal</code>, the token reference is a <code>qds-tabs</code> with a
    <code>qds-input</code> filter, and every color comes from a semantic token,
    so if a token is wrong, these pages show it. Try the theme toggle.
  </p>

  {% example "A few of the components" %}
    <qds-stack gap="400">
      <qds-stack direction="inline" gap="200" align="center" wrap>
        <qds-button>Save</qds-button>
        <qds-button variant="secondary">Cancel</qds-button>
        <qds-chip variant="success">Published</qds-chip>
        <qds-toggle checked>Notifications</qds-toggle>
      </qds-stack>
      <qds-progress-bar label="Upload progress" value="64"></qds-progress-bar>
    </qds-stack>
  {% endexample %}

  <p><a href="/components/">Every component, with a playground</a></p>
</section>

<section class="home-band">
  <h2>Restyle with one variable</h2>
  <p class="home-band__lede">
    A component reads only its own tokens, and each one aliases a semantic token,
    so it follows the theme. Override one, on one instance or a whole page, and
    nothing else needs to change.
  </p>

  {% example "One component token, overridden" %}
    <qds-stack direction="inline" gap="300" wrap>
      <qds-button>Default</qds-button>
      <qds-button style="
        --qds-component-button-primary-color-background-rest: var(--qds-color-purple-600);
        --qds-component-button-primary-color-background-hover: var(--qds-color-purple-700);
        --qds-component-button-primary-color-background-active: var(--qds-color-purple-800);
      ">Restyled</qds-button>
    </qds-stack>
  {% endexample %}

  <p><a href="/foundations/tokens/">How the three token tiers fit together</a></p>
</section>

<section class="home-band">
  <h2>Get started</h2>

  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      <p>Install the components. The tokens come with them:</p>
      <pre><code>npm install @quieto/ui</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>Load the tokens once, at the top of your app, then register the components:</p>
      <pre><code>import '@quieto/design-tokens/css';
import '@quieto/ui';</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>Use them like any HTML element:</p>
      <pre><code>&lt;qds-button variant="secondary"&gt;Cancel&lt;/qds-button&gt;</code></pre>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p>
    Without the token stylesheet the components still render, from fallbacks
    built into each one, but nothing follows the theme.
  </p>
</section>
